  "modifications": "Selected mechanics reimplemented in Python; original example actors and prompts. No source art, setting, or full rulebook is bundled.",
  "narrator_instructions": "Selected system: SRD 5.2.1 example, version 0.3.0.\nUse ability_check, saving_throw, or attack for rolls. Ability scores, proficiency, weapon data,\nand AC come from stored actor stats. The GM supplies the check difficulty and circumstances in\nvalidated input. Narrate the recorded resolution. Natural 1/20 overrides apply to attacks only.\nUse damage or heal for GM-declared hit point changes; HP is clamped to 0..max and nothing happens\nautomatically at 0 HP. Use apply_condition or remove_condition to change named conditions\nexplicitly; conditions have no mechanical effect on rolls in this example. Use advance_time to\nmove simulated time in rounds, minutes, hours, or days. Use give or take to change an actor's\nexact item counts; item keys are lowercase snake_case, items have no modelled effect, and taking\nmore than is held is rejected. The recorded inventory is authoritative; never invent items.\nUnsupported rules require a future implementation; never borrow Fate rules or invent their effects.\n",
  "not_implemented": [
    "character creation and advancement",
    "classes and spells",
    "initiative, range, movement and action economy",
    "resistances and vulnerabilities",
    "death saves, instant death and automatic unconsciousness",
    "condition effects on rolls and condition durations",
    "item effects, equipment, weight and currency",
    "inspiration and rules rerolls"
  ],
